{"id":"u-b3d1468a-ace6-440a-889e-11c7c47c47fe","src":"community","title":"Rocky III & IV Physique workout","author":"Reyes Saúl  F.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/Uv5zcj-rocky-iii-and-iv-physique-workout","desc":"Unleash your inner champion with the Rocky III & IV Physique workout, a comprehensive 12-week program designed to sculpt your body like a true athlete. With 48 intense sessions, you'll engage in a variety of advanced exercises targeting strength, muscle growth, and athletic performance, all within a full gym setting. Each 60-minute workout is crafted to challenge your limits, featuring key movements like the Incline Bench Press, Pull-Ups, and Romanian Deadlifts. Prepare to transform your physique and build the resilience of a champion! \n\n\nConditioning (2–3 Times Per Week)\n\n- Jump Rope: 10–15 minutes\n- Shadowboxing: 4–6 rounds\n- Easy Run: 20–30 minutes\n- Sprints: 6–10 × 50–100 meters (optional, once weekly)\n\n---\n\nProgression\n\n- Start with a weight you can lift with good technique.\n- Leave 1–2 reps in reserve (RIR) on most sets.\n- When you reach the top of the rep range on every set, increase the weight by 2.5–5%.\n- Focus on controlled lowering (2–3 seconds) and explosive lifting.\n- Rest 2–3 minutes for compound lifts and 60–90 seconds for isolation exercises.\n\n🍽️ Nutrition Guide\n\nPhase 1 – Lean Bulk (12–24 Weeks)\n\nGoal\n\nBuild muscle while keeping fat gain to a minimum.\n\nCalories\n\n- Eat 250–350 calories above maintenance each day.\n\nProtein\n\n- 1.6–2.2 g per kg of body weight\n\nFat\n\n- 0.6–1.0 g per kg of body weight\n\nCarbohydrates\n\n- Fill the rest of your calories with carbohydrates to fuel training and recovery.\n\nFood Choices\n\n- Lean meats (chicken, turkey, lean beef, fish)\n- Eggs\n- Greek yogurt\n- Rice\n- Potatoes\n- Oats\n- Whole-grain bread\n- Fruits and vegetables\n- Nuts and olive oil\n\nRate of Gain\n\nAim to gain 0.25–0.5% of your body weight per week. If you're gaining faster, reduce calories slightly.\n\n---\n\nPhase 2 – Cutting (8–12 Weeks)\n\nGoal\n\nReveal muscle definition while maintaining strength and muscle mass.\n\nCalories\n\n- Eat 300–500 calories below maintenance each day.\n\nProtein\n\n- 2.0–2.4 g per kg of body weight\n\nFat\n\n- 0.6–0.8 g per kg of body weight\n\nCarbohydrates\n\n- Use the remaining calories for carbohydrates to support training performance.\n\nCardio\n\n- 2–4 sessions per week\n- 20–30 minutes of incline walking, jogging, jump rope, or cycling.\n- Keep lifting heavy to preserve muscle.\n\nRate of Loss\n\nAim to lose 0.5–1.0% of your body weight per week.\n\n---\n\nHydration\n\n- Drink 2.5–4 liters of water daily.\n- Increase water intake during hot weather or intense conditioning sessions.\n\n---\n\nSupplements (Optional)\n\n- Whey Protein\n- Creatine Monohydrate (5 g/day)\n- Caffeine (before training if desired)\n- Fish Oil (Omega-3)\n- Vitamin D (if deficient)\n\n---\n\nRocky Mindset\n\n«Bulk to build. Cut to reveal.\n\n- sleep 7–9 hours each night.\n\n---\n\nRocky Rules\n\n- Train with intensity, not ego.\n- Master perfect technique before adding weight.\n- Be consistent every week.\n- Never skip conditioning.\n- Recovery is part of training.\n- Build strength, athleticism, and discipline—not just muscle.","level":["Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-21T01:17:50.622Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadli